e":"MXLStaffDetails","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLStaffDetails","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The staff-details element is used to indicate different types of staves. The optional number attribute"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specifies the staff number from top to bottom on the system, as with clef. The print-object attribute is used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"to indicate when a staff is not printed in a part, usually in large scores where empty parts are omitted. It"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is yes by default. If print-spacing is yes while print-object is no, the score is printed in cutaway format"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"where vertical space is left for the empty part."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlstaffdetails","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLStaffDetails","role":"symbol"}}}